dedb (0.0.15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Each command now installs its own man page (dedb-run(1),
    dedb-import(1), dedb-dosboxconf(1), ...) alongside dedb(1).
  * Error handling reworked: the library modules raise plain exceptions
    and only the command layer turns them into messages, so a failure
    such as an unknown game or a game that isn't downloaded prints a
    one-line error rather than a traceback. `dedb <cmd> -b <unknown>`,
    and passing both a `<scheme>://` URL and `-b`, now exit 1 (was 2).
  * Internal cli.py cleanup. No other command-line or output changes.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:55:00 +0100

dedb (0.0.14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * dosbox.conf parser rewritten: `%` in values is kept verbatim
    (previously mangled), and quoted values are handled consistently.
  * DOSBox->DOSEMU2 conversion reworked as a three-model translation
    pipeline (parsed config -> DOSBox model -> DOSEMU2 model), with the
    per-field translations expressed as validators on the model.
  * autoexec handling is now a declarative routing table rather than
    branching code.
  * No command-line or output changes; this is an internal cleanup
    release on top of 0.0.13.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 23:05:10 +0100

dedb (0.0.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New `dedb dosemuconf` command: shows the converted DOSEMU2 output
    (`dosemu.conf` + `userhook.bat`) from dosbox.conf paths or a
    `gog:` / `archive:` game, the DOSEMU2-side mirror of `dosboxconf`.
  * `dedb import` now also accepts dosbox.conf paths (merged, written to
    `--output-dir`), replacing the separate `importdosbox` command.
  * `dedb import` loses `--dumpconf` / `--dumpuserhook` - use
    `dedb dosemuconf` instead.
  * The DOSBox->DOSEMU2 conversion engine moved to a standalone
    `dedb.convert` library; `import` moved to a new `dedb.dosemu` app.
    If you have pinned `apps` in dedbconf.toml, add `"dedb.dosemu"`.
  * `--cmdline` on `dedb run --dosbox|--dosemu` (and on `dosboxconf` /
    `dosemuconf`) prints the emulator command that would run - a
    shell-pasteable line - and stops, with no launch or conversion.
  * `dedb run --dosemu` no longer writes `userhook.bat` into the game
    directory - it is staged in a dedb-owned dir mounted as its own
    DOSEMU2 drive, keeping the downloaded game immutable.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Wed, 03 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0100

dedb (0.0.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Shell tab completion. The package installs completion scripts for
    bash, zsh and fish; `dedb completion <shell>` prints the script for
    a pip install. GAME arguments complete to `gog:<id>` / `archive:<id>`
    targets from local data - downloaded games, the GOG owned-games
    cache and the archive.org metadata cache - with no network access.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Wed, 03 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0100

dedb (0.0.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * `dedb dosboxconf` now works for `archive://` items, rendered from
    archive.org's launch metadata - no dosbox.conf needed. The item
    must be downloaded first.
  * `dedb dosboxconf` accepts the `gog:<id>` / `archive:<id>` colon form,
    not only `<scheme>://<id>`.
  * `dedb ls` filters backends with `-b` / `--backend` instead of
    `--type`, matching `run` / `download` / `import` / `rm`.
  * archive.org items are converted through the same model pipeline as
    GOG games (the DOSBox command line emularity synthesises from
    `emulator_start`); generated output is unchanged.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0100

dedb (0.0.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename the [archive] `favorites_user` setting to `archive_user`. An
    old `favorites_user` line is ignored - rename it by hand.
  * A fresh dedbconf.toml no longer pins `apps`, so apps added in a later
    dedb are picked up without editing the config.
  * `dedb --help` lists the cross-cutting commands under "Commands:"
    instead of a "[dedb]" group.
  * Bring doc/ and ARCHITECTURE.md up to date.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 03:15:00 +0100

dedb (0.0.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New `dedb refreshmetadata [GAME]...`: re-fetch backend metadata and
    rewrite each metadata.json without re-downloading the game. With no
    GAME it does this for every downloaded game.
  * `dedb download`, `import` and `rm` now take more than one GAME.
  * `dedb rm` accepts shell wildcards matched against downloaded names
    (e.g. `dedb rm 'gog:tyrian*'`), and asks once to confirm the set.
  * `dedb ls -v`: a column view (target, title, classification,
    converted?, launch profiles).
  * metadata.json is now one versioned envelope shared by both backends;
    existing downloads are upgraded in place on the next download,
    import or refreshmetadata, with no re-download.
  * `dedb refreshmetadata` and `dedb download --refreshmetadata` no
    longer do a per-game GOG library lookup - the product id comes from
    the existing metadata.json.
  * Add ARCHITECTURE.md.
  * Skip the test suite during the Debian package build; it runs in CI.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 02:47:00 +0100

dedb (0.0.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add `dedb lsarchive`: list an archive.org user's public favorites as
    `archive:<id>` targets, filtered to MS-DOS items by default (--all
    for every favorite, -1 for bare lines). The username comes from the
    new `[archive]` favorites_user setting, or is prompted for and
    optionally saved when unset.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:26:00 +0100

dedb (0.0.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix every `dedb run ... --dosemu`: stop emitting `$_video = "X"` into
    the generated dosemu.conf. dosemu2's $_video is the emulated video
    adapter style, not a display backend, and the bogus value aborted
    dosemu2 at startup.
  * Regenerate the DOSEMU2 config on every launch, so a config written by
    an older dedb no longer lingers.
  * Fix `dedb import` crashing with a convert() TypeError before writing
    any config.

 -- Stuart Axon <stu.axon@gmail.com>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:08:38 +0100

